WF-03 — Personalized Accessibility Search and Surrounding Exploration
Read Part A for destination discovery, explicit needs, scope limits and user-facing outcomes. System Diagrams is the shared visual baseline; Part B owns deterministic matching and APIs. Appendix D identifies the matching shared figures and compatible data view.
Contract baseline: AMVN-BE-2026-11-14-r2. Freeze scope: WF-01 through Admin Portal; implementation follows the owning Part B and shared bindings.
Implementation lookup: preferences/favorites/public media B.1; predicate and scope evaluation B.2; validation B.3; query/sort/cursor B.4; endpoints B.5; configuration B.6; failures/privacy B.7–B.8; acceptance B.9. WF1 owns published facts and identity; WF2 owns freshness/review state. Search reads these contracts without creating evidence.

Part A — Technical / Design Specification
A.1 Purpose, scope and interpretation
A.1.1 Purpose
Help a User find places, inspect published accessibility features and approved public evidence, and obtain a need-specific summary when scoped evidence supports it. The User may search by name/address, use Find near me, or select an area/pin. Opening a result never creates or changes a Location, Submission, claim, vote or reward.
A.1.2 Scope and workflow ownership
WF-03 owns accessibility discovery through POST /api/v1/locations/discover/search and local place suggestions through GET /api/v1/locations/search?source=accessmap. Only AccessMap identities and current published scoped features appear in WF3 results; third-party place candidates are not mixed into these results. WF-01 owns evidence contribution, resolves an already imported local OSM identity or explicit User proposal, and owns the separate controlled OSM importer. Search/submit never performs an on-demand external place lookup. WF-02 owns votes, inaccuracy reports, disputes and freshness. The main audience is wheelchair users and people with mobility limitations; elderly people and stroller users may select the same concrete feature criteria. Mobility presets are wheelchair, limited_mobility, elderly, stroller and none. A result supports destination choice; it does not provide indoor/turn-by-turn navigation or guarantee a usable route.
A.1.3 Boundaries
WF-01 owns canonical Location identity, deduplication, immutable evidence, publication and LocationFeature truth. WF-02 owns votes/reports, disputes and freshness. WF-03 reads their published/public-safe outputs and evaluates explicit current search conditions. A contribution, vote or report starts only after a separate User action. External geocoding may resolve a User-selected center; an external place listing is never a WF3 destination result or accessibility source.
A.2 Actors and responsibilities
Guest and User search by text, current position, selected address/area or manual pin, set explicit mobility conditions and inspect published facts without mandatory login. User means isAdmin=false and may separately contribute, vote or report after authentication. Guest selecting a protected action is asked to register/sign in with bounded draft context retained. Saved needs/favorites require the authenticated owner; current criteria work without a profile. Admin signs in only to the ReactJS Admin Portal and maintains implemented mappings/defaults under current isAdmin=true and portal authorization. Admin credentials do not establish a mobile User session. ASP.NET Core validates queries, reads PostGIS and applies deterministic matching; optional geocoding is outside the DB transaction. Python analyzes contribution evidence in WF-01 and is not called for search matching. Reuse WF-01 A.2.3 User.isAdmin access rules.
A.3 Architecture and data flow
A.3.1 Logical architecture
React Native → ASP.NET Core search/discovery services → PostgreSQL/PostGIS Location, current scoped LocationFeature and WF2 public-safe state. WF3 text suggestions explicitly request source=accessmap, which skips external place fallback. Optional address geocoding only establishes a center after the User selects an unambiguous address; manual pin placement requires no geocoder. A versioned .NET rule policy matches published features. Evidence previews reuse approved public media derivatives through short-lived permitted links; raw storage keys and private originals are never returned.
A.3.2 Search-time policy
MatchingPolicy v1 is a deterministic, versioned backend rule policy over published scoped features and the User's visible required/preferred conditions. There is no remote AI matcher or alternate matching adapter in this release. Unavailable required data yields InsufficientData; if the local matching component fails while published details remain available, return the checklist with label=null and degraded=true. Do not turn a failure into an accessibility verdict. A label describes the selected conditions and evidence time, not whole-place regulatory compliance.
A.4 Preconditions, product actions and outcomes
A.4.1 Preconditions and successful outcome
Text search requires q and can run without GPS; it has no implicit 2,000 m cutoff. Find near me requires a valid center and starts at configurable 2,000 m. A manual area/pin uses the displayed confirmed radius. Optional coordinates can bias ranking. Results are bounded and paginated; default discovery pageSize=20 with configured maximum. Guest and User can search/discover using explicit current filters without logging in or saving a profile. Saved preferences/favorites remain owner-only.
A.4.2 Product action mapping
The following product actions map to backend behavior; identifiers of actual Figma screens are intentionally not assumed.

A.4.3 Business rules and validation outcomes
Distinguish invalid input, missing published evidence and unavailable support services. No missing evidence or service failure can establish Inaccessible. Feature type is the supported category, filter is the User's requested condition, and SubmissionClaim is a separate evidence-backed assertion confirmed in WF1.

A.5 Search identity and spatial resolution
A.5.1 Local lookup and contribution handoff
WF3 calls GET /api/v1/locations/search with source=accessmap. The shared backend applies local name/address matching only. source omitted and source=accessmap are equivalent local-only requests in both WF1 and WF3; unsupported sources return422. Empty results never invoke Overpass, Google or another place provider, enqueue an import or create a Location. Controlled OSM import and an explicit User proposal are separate WF1 operations. The selector is not an authorization boundary. Suggestion GET returns identities and safe hasAccessibilityData, never compatibility labels. POST /api/v1/locations/discover/search evaluates only Active local destinations using current published scoped features. Public visibility rules still apply to every identity; Provisional may only be an allowed identity suggestion, with no trusted label, and never a discovery recommendation. Hidden places are never exposed by Guest or User public search; Merged identities resolve to the canonical target.
When a place lacks evidence or local search is empty, offer Contribute accessibility information. Retain bounded canonical LocationId/name/address/pin, selected scope and missing-feature prompts. Guest must register/sign in as User before upload or submission, then resume the retained draft; navigation alone creates no Location or Submission. WF-01 independently resolves identity, deduplicates and requires evidence plus explicit claim confirmation. Search filters, companion/floor context never become claims automatically.
Map layers remain bounded by viewport/bbox and zoom, with clustering, pagination and explicit enabled layers. PostGIS stores/queries the spatial records; the selected map SDK renders them. Only approved published features/entrances/advisories and permitted sourced context are displayed; never load all places or raw media.
A.5.2 GPS and manual address
q is the search string for a place name or address, not a coordinate. The User may choose current position, select an unambiguous address/area result, or tap/drag a map pin; the UI extracts latitude/longitude so the User never needs to type them. A pin selected as search center is not evidence of a visit and does not update Location.Position. Validate finite latitude in [-90,90], longitude in [-180,180] and a complete pair when supplied. With q and no explicitly selected radius, search local text matches without an implicit 2 km restriction; optional coordinates only bias proximity. With no q, coordinates define nearby search and an omitted radius uses the 2,000 m Find near me default. Discovery sends the selected center and explicit area radius. A typed address is not silently geocoded to an ambiguous location; ask the User to choose or place a pin. GPS denial leaves text and manual-center search available.
A.6 Published features, matching and labels
A.6.1 Data authority
Read current published LocationFeature and source/version within (LocationId, ScopeId, FeatureType), never a pending/rejected raw claim. Location.Status already distinguishes Provisional, Active, Merged and Hidden; do not add another visibility column for the same purpose. Discovery uses Active local destinations; an allowed Provisional identity suggestion has hasAccessibilityData=false and label=null, while Hidden is excluded and Merged resolves to canonical identity. Public visibility does not determine whether a place exists for deduplication: WF1's server-side identity check must search eligible canonical/provisional duplicate candidates even when they are absent from the public result. Reuse a confirmed Provisional match; an overlapping Hidden place requires authorized review rather than a duplicate or automatic unhide. Do not disclose hidden/private metadata in that response. WF2 may attach a freshness warning, dispute or time-bounded advisory, but only WF1 publication changes the feature value.
A.6.2 Profile-to-feature mapping
Supported feature types reuse WF1: Ramp, EntranceDoor (including measured clear opening width), Elevator, AccessibleRestroom. User selects implemented types only; there is no Other. Categories, desired-state filters and evidence-backed claims remain distinct. A new type requires a versioned scope/evidence/matching change. An image or demographic preset cannot establish whole-place accessibility.
Editable presets within the four-feature catalogue: wheelchair requires EntranceDoor and prefers Ramp/Elevator/AccessibleRestroom; limited_mobility, elderly and stroller have no required default and prefer EntranceDoor/Ramp/Elevator; none has no defaults. User sees, edits and confirms every requirement. Elevator is required only when the User explicitly selects it; ground-floor venues do not fail merely for lacking one. Required criteria use AND within one Known physical scope; preferred criteria affect discovery ranking only. Missing, unmeasured, stale or disputed required evidence yields InsufficientData. EntranceDoor=Available never proves an entire step-free journey. No implicit feature inheritance across floors/entrances or demographic weights. requested desiredStatus=Available is supported; other desired states return 422 UNSUPPORTED_DESIRED_STATUS, while actual Limited/NotAvailable/Unknown remain visible. Display settings do not change matching.
A.6.3 Label precedence
A result summarizes the User's explicit required conditions within one confirmed scope. Prefer a fully supported independent context; missing or uncertain evidence gives InsufficientData. Inaccessible requires affirmative failure in every relevant documented context. Preferred features affect ranking only; no required conditions gives label=null.
The baseline has no typed assistance representation, so it does not emit AssistedAccess. A companion toggle or Limited status alone cannot establish assistance. B.2 owns predicate evaluation, scope/floor restrictions and label precedence; A.6.2 explains editable presets.
A.6.4 Confidence and regulatory claims
WF1 FeatureConfidence is advisory evidence confidence, not probability of independent whole-place access or a regulatory compliance score. QCVN comparison follows WF1 B.3.8.1's ten selected criteria under qcvn10-2024-accessmap-v1. Only reviewed source-linked measurements support a Meets/DoesNotMeet result; an unmeasured door remains InsufficientEvidence. Do not apply 900 mm to restroom doors or interior doors: CriterionCode and physical scope determine applicability. Discovery continues to use its explicit same-scope feature predicates/limits; it must not silently add a universal QCVN gate or equate missing comparisons with NotAvailable.
A.7 Surrounding-area context and media
Evidence thumbnails are approved public preview images derived from media supporting published accessibility information. They are not private originals, raw object keys or unreviewed uploads. Reuse the existing WF1 media/storage pipeline; do not require a new LocationVisualCache table. A thumbnail link may be renewed after expiry only after rechecking that its source remains public and permitted. Public previews retain safe source/observation time while excluding private capture/device GPS.
SurroundingObservation remains optional sourced context with source, captured time, permission and expiry; return an empty observations list when no supported source exists. Cache expiry does not make an old physical observation current. If a source changes, use a newly accepted observation/version and update the projection through its existing authorized path; do not overwrite verified accessibility facts from an external context feed. See B.1 for request timeout, link renewal and cache invalidation rules.
A.8 API and response contract
A.8.1 Endpoints and ownership
Guest or User calls GET /api/v1/locations/search?source=accessmap for local suggestions, POST /api/v1/locations/discover/search for explicit current-condition matching and bounded map/detail/surroundings reads. These public read-only operations accept anonymous requests; POST discovery does not persist a business mutation. Suggestion GET accepts q or coordinates and returns no compatibility label; discovery uses current published local scoped evidence. source=accessmap suppresses external place results. Geocoding only resolves a chosen center. Reads/navigation never create Location, claim, vote or report.
Saved needs and favorites require an active authenticated owner with isAdmin=false: GET/PUT/DELETE /api/v1/me/accessibility-preference and favorites routes derive UserId from the session. Preference GET returns defaults/version/consentedAt or 404 unset; PUT validates supported criteria, consent and expectedVersion (409 stale, 422 invalid); DELETE clears idempotently. Favorites are bounded, paginated and owner-only. Guest search/discovery/map/published detail calls succeed without a token; Guest private-account or write calls return 401. A different User cannot read another owner's resources. Saved defaults may prefill the UI visibly; the backend evaluates only explicit discovery criteria.

A.8.2 User-facing result fields
Suggestion DTO: source=accessmap, local locationId, name/address, public place coordinate and hasAccessibilityData; no externalPlaceId or compatibility label in WF3 responses. Discovery DTO: locationId, label/reasons, per-condition scoped evidence/version/verified time, verified entrance/floor limits, WF2 safe freshness/advisory flags, matchingPolicyVersion, approved public evidence thumbnail and nextCursor. Map DTOs expose bounded approved marker/cluster IDs, source/version and safe counts. A thumbnail is a permitted public derivative, not an authorization bypass to a private original. Never return private user/device GPS, account identity, report notes, storage keys or provider secrets.
A.8.3 Failure and fallback semantics
400 when suggestion search has neither q nor a complete coordinate pair, or malformed coordinates; 422 for invalid radius, source selector or unsupported/duplicate discovery criteria. Text search without GPS is valid. Return 200 with empty local results when no place matches; known places with insufficient relevant published evidence remain explicitly InsufficientData, not Inaccessible. A local matching failure can degrade to a published checklist with label=null only when the published data read succeeded; a failed data read returns a typed service error. Geocoder failure retains available local text results and offers manual pin selection; it never triggers external destination fallback. Never silently choose an ambiguous center.
A.9 User sequence
1. Guest or User opens search; current filters work without login. Only an authenticated owner can load saved defaults/favorites. 2. Enter q, choose Find near me, select an address/area or place a pin; text search has no implicit 2 km cutoff. 3. Local suggestions and discovery evaluate the explicit supported criteria against published scoped facts. 4. Show reasons, freshness, approved previews and access limits; missing required evidence is InsufficientData. 5. Read only enabled approved map layers in the viewport. 6. Guest choosing Contribute, Vote or Report is prompted to register/sign in as User, then resumes bounded retained context. Search filters are never preconfirmed claims; WF-01 independently validates evidence and Submit. WF-02 participation remains a separate authenticated action.
A.10 Exceptions
No q/center: prompt for text, address/area or manual pin. No saved profile: use explicit current criteria or show the general checklist. Missing published criteria: identify the missing feature/scope, show InsufficientData and offer WF1 contribution. An invalid catalogue value returns typed validation, rather than substituting another need. Local matching failure degrades only to an available published checklist. Geocoding/provider failure means that address-resolution call failed or timed out; retain local text results/selected pin and offer retry or manual selection, without adding external destinations.
Stale/disputed data is owned by WF2. Its freshness reader/jobs flag NeedsRecheck; Users may submit eligible confirmations or reports, and Admin reviews disputes/evidence/advisories. An evidence-backed factual correction goes through WF1 publication to create a new feature version. WF3 reads the public-safe state, displays the warning and withholds a strong compatibility conclusion if a required feature is affected; search never resolves a dispute or overwrites published truth.
A.11 Privacy, accessibility and reliability
Process the chosen center and current criteria for the request; do not persist raw queries, GPS trails or inferred visit habits as a server-side search history. Redact these inputs from logs/analytics. Saved needs and favorites are optional, private, owner-controlled and deletable; they are explicit records, not inferred behavior. Recent places stay on the device, at most 20 canonical references, clearable and expiring after 30 days; no server synchronization or route history.
Matching uses User-confirmed functional needs and current conditions. The current policy defines no age/gender scoring coefficients or demographic-based verdict. It does not infer those attributes from behavior or require demographic UI classifications. Changing this later would require an explicit versioned data/matching contract; this revision adds no demographic fields. Keep labels explanatory, controls readable and usable, and do not rely on color alone. Larger text/contrast settings do not affect ranking. Bound geocoding timeouts, explicit search areas, page sizes and map viewport loads. Cache only permitted public/versioned data and invalidate it after publication or relevant WF2 state changes.
A.12 Acceptance outcomes
Guest and User can search by q/manual pin without login or GPS. Find near me starts at 2,000 m; text matches outside it remain searchable unless an explicit radius is selected. WF-03 returns only permitted local identities and published scoped facts. Public search/discovery/map/detail/history and approved evidence projections return no private account, report, media-key or device-GPS data. Guest writes and /me routes return 401; registration/sign-in permits a normal User to continue. Unsupported filters fail validation; missing evidence remains InsufficientData. Backend rules match without remote AI. Contribution retains bounded draft context, never promotes filters to claims. Existing safe-cache, scoped-version and 20-item/30-day/local Clear rules remain.
A.13 Baseline decisions and deferred capabilities
MatchingPolicy v1, explicit filters, request-only companion/floor context, anonymous Guest search/view and authenticated opt-in saved defaults are the approved baseline. Missing scoped evidence yields InsufficientData. Unsupported metrics, future profile categories and inferred habits remain excluded.

Part B — Implementation Specification
B.0 Implementation authority
Part B defines the WF3 contract using WF1 published data and WF2 public-safe freshness/review state. The approved release uses deterministic backend matching, the supported mobility catalogue and explicit current-request filters. A.13 records remaining configuration/deferred items, not permission to enable unsupported mechanisms. Search and navigation do not create or mutate trusted accessibility facts. The three-metric policy does not change discovery suitability ranking. Display only publication-safe feature confidence and ConfidenceMode; missing confidence is unknown, never zero accuracy. AccountStandingScore, ContributionAccuracyRate and ReputationPoints are account measures, not place-accessibility labels or ranking inputs. ContributionAccuracyRate displays only assessed contribution claims; reports and comments are excluded. A comment report does not change a place's confidence or discovery rank; only approved comment visibility follows WF2 moderation.
Cross-workflow implementation baseline: create this module within the new .NET8 Code First solution under WF1 B.0.3–B.0.13. Use the shared defined User/auth, DbContext, repository/UoW, storage, jobs and outbox once; there is no old solution or backfill. Apply Worker→Internal Job API, typed DTOs, configuration, DI, generic bases, scoped IUnitOfWork facade and executable acceptance. The owning Part B defines business policies, routes, final schema and retry budgets. Scenario IDs replace diagram-pair numbering. All SQL/EF business access is API-side; scheduler storage is separately credentialed. Include the module in S01–S08 checkpointed generation and the complete test matrix.
B.1 Core entities and read models
Reuse existing Location, AccessScope, current LocationFeature/history, approved SubmissionMedia derivatives and WF2 FeatureCommunityState/TemporaryAccessAdvisory. No new User/Location or required LocationVisualCache table is introduced. Current search requests are transient; server-side query/GPS trails and habit learning are outside this release.
B.1.1 Saved needs, favorites and local recent places
AccessibilityPreference is one optional private row per UserId: supported mobility profile, defaultRequiredFeatures/defaultPreferredFeatures, consent timestamp, UpdatedAt and Version. Validate canonical featureType/desiredStatus pairs, no duplicates, and explicit required/preferred lists. GET/PUT/DELETE enforce session ownership, consent and optimistic version. Do not persist the current center, companion toggle or requested floor in this row; this release adds no age/gender matching fields. A single search can override defaults visibly without rewriting them. Persist only desiredStatus=Available under MatchingPolicy v1. Existing unsupported saved criteria require explicit User reconfirmation/editing before reuse; never silently reinterpret them.
FavoriteLocation stores UserId, canonical Active LocationId and CreatedAt with unique(UserId,LocationId), configurable maximum 100 and owner-only deletion. CreatedAt is the first successful save time, supports newest-saved ordering and stable pagination (CreatedAt DESC, LocationId DESC), and is not a visit time. Idempotent repeated PUT does not move CreatedAt. Resolve merged IDs on write; hide inactive/unapproved favorites on public-detail reads while allowing removal.
Merge handling uses WF1 B.7.2's canonical resolver and explicit scope map. The merge transaction deduplicates favorites at the canonical Location and preserves earliest CreatedAt; reads/removal of old references resolve consistently.
Recent places are device-local, deduplicated canonical references, most recently opened first; keep at most 20 and expire an entry 30 days after its latest open. Clear removes the local list. Retain only the reference and local recency metadata needed for this shortcut; no server sync, raw search query or GPS trail.
B.1.2 Public media, optional observations and cache renewal
Reuse the approved public-media projection in WF1 B.18.4. Resolve source media/original hash to a Ready derivative manifest in AIAnalysis.RawResultJson.backendEvaluation.publicMedia; never expose the raw SubmissionMedia.StorageKey or create a separate derivative store. A timeout is a failed call, not media expiry. For an expired signed link, recheck publication, approved source, Ready status and permissions before renewing the capability. Renewal changes neither observation time nor accessibility confidence.
No LocationVisualCache table is required. If a public projection is cached, bind it to current scoped LocationFeature version, relevant WF2 assessment/advisory state and policy version. Publication or WF2 state changes invalidate/rebuild affected projections through existing signals or a read-time version check. An expired/mismatched cache entry is recomputed on demand from authorized current sources, not silently extended. If refresh fails, omit/mark the optional context unavailable; it cannot support a positive label.
Optional SurroundingObservation carries LocationId, source, captured time, geometry/media reference, permission and expiry under its existing source contract. Expiry makes the observation stale; only newly accepted source evidence can make it current. A context-source change updates the projection after its authorized ingestion/review, never overwrites WF1 verified feature truth. Return an empty observations list if the optional source is not implemented.
B.1.3 Enum catalogue and wire values
Mobility profile values: none, wheelchair, limited_mobility, elderly, stroller. These are editable filter presets, not separate User roles.
Matching label values: IndependentAccess, AssistedAccess, Inaccessible, InsufficientData; label=null when no personalized conclusion is requested or matching is degraded. AssistedAccess is retained but not emitted by this baseline because the existing contract lacks typed verified-assistance data; follow A.6.3. Lowercase explanatory wording is not another stored enum.
Use WF1 fixed feature enum identities Ramp1,Elevator2,AccessibleRestroom3,EntranceDoor5. InitialCreate/seed has exactly this active catalogue; unsupported values are rejected. No legacy saved-needs reconciliation or compatibility alias is generated.
Reuse WF1 FeatureClaimStatus: Unknown, Available, Limited, NotAvailable. Unknown never means a negative observation.
Reuse WF1 LocationStatus: Provisional, Active, Merged, Hidden; AccessScope.Kind: BuildingGeneral, Entrance, Floor, Unit; CoverageStatus: Known, Unknown. Known confirms physical scope identity through existing Admin review, not accessibility or complete coverage; each Floor scope represents one FloorNumber. Reuse WF-01 B.3.1 confirmation/audit and existing position states rather than define another enum or workflow. Include Closed=4 under the WF1-compatible enum. Active discovery excludes Closed identities and all retired current features; direct safe history reads can explain closure/replacement with an explicit successor link. MapLibre+OpenFreeMap renders base tiles independently of local POI results. Empty PostGIS suggestions return200 empty; permit explicit authenticated name/pin proposal. No Overpass/Google search fallback. Tile POIs and app database identities need not coincide; no basemap label is trusted accessibility evidence.
Reuse WF2 FeatureCommunityLabel: Uncorroborated, Fresh, Reinforced, NeedsRecheck, ConflictReported, CommunityUnderReview, plus existing advisory status. WF3 reads these flags; it does not own their transitions. Do not redeclare shared enum numeric IDs or accept arbitrary feature names.
B.2 Profile matching contract
Discovery evaluates current published LocationFeature versions and evidence per canonical Location/Scope/FeatureType with WF-02 public-safe state and matchingPolicyVersion. Guest and User supply explicit required/preferred criteria, companion/floor context and selected area. Saved preferences may prefill only for an authenticated consenting owner; they never silently alter a request. Guest search needs no saved profile.
Current release context rule: one candidate context is exactly one canonical AccessScope returned by WF1's reviewed merge/scope resolver with CoverageStatus=Known. Required predicates must all be satisfied from current published features in that same ScopeId. Do not combine sibling scopes, inherit parent/BuildingGeneral facts or infer connectivity. requestedFloor restricts candidates to confirmed Floor scopes with exactly that FloorNumber; unsupported/unknown floor scope leaves the request InsufficientData. Without requestedFloor, evaluate each documented same-scope context independently and expose its scope/limits. An Entrance result establishes only that entrance's documented context, never a route to a floor. A wide entrance and an elevator on Floor 2 are insufficient together without a single supported context. Unknown scope identity cannot support a strong positive/negative conclusion. Return per-condition reasons and ScopeId. Cross-scope connectivity is outside this release and requires a separate typed evidence contract. WF1 B.3.1 owns scope-identity confirmation in existing Admin review. Matching never changes CoverageStatus; historical published data still under Unknown remains unresolved/InsufficientData until reviewed. It cannot silently become Known or inherit facts from another scope.
A historical source scope mapped by a merge is resolved to its reviewed canonical target; it is not an additional independent context. This rule derives scope selection from the merge mapping and introduces no separate AccessScope retirement flag.
Evaluate one confirmed canonical ScopeId at a time under the preceding context rule.
Required predicates: desiredStatus must be Available. Current same-context Available with adequate evidence and represented limits satisfies the predicate. Affirmative current NotAvailable fails it. Missing, Unknown, stale, disputed, unmeasured or unrepresented Limited evidence is unresolved; a versioned typed measurement rule may establish Limited satisfaction/failure where implemented.
Context result: all required predicates satisfied → independent context; any affirmative failed predicate → ruled-out context; otherwise unresolved. Across contexts prefer IndependentAccess, otherwise InsufficientData if any relevant alternative remains unresolved, otherwise Inaccessible only when every relevant documented context is affirmatively ruled out. No-required requests return label=null.
Preferred criteria rank satisfied evidence only. AssistedAccess is retained vocabulary but is not emitted by this baseline; neither companion context, Limited, text nor images encode an assistance option. Output scoped reasons and evidence/source versions. Future request predicates require a separately defined policy.
Age/gender have no assigned fields, coefficients or demographic verdict in the current contract. User-confirmed functional conditions govern this release; display settings, favorites, local recency and visit frequency do not serve as accessibility evidence or inferred requirements.
B.3 Validation and service boundaries
Validate q or a complete coordinate pair, source=accessmap when called from WF3, explicit area/radius where relevant, canonical filters and bounded page/row counts. Reject unsupported source/filter values with typed validation. source=accessmap must bypass external place lookup, including on an empty local page; it does not bypass visibility. Geocode only a selected address when needed and outside any DB transaction; a selected pin supplies its coordinates directly. Use deterministic local backend rules for matching. Python remains in WF1 evidence processing, with no remote matching request or private-profile/media transfer from WF3. If a local policy error occurs, degrade only to available published data, never a fabricated label.
B.4 Search query and sorting
Suggestion GET: with q, match normalized local place name/address; do not apply a 2 km filter unless the User explicitly selected a radius. Optional coordinates supply proximity bias after textual relevance. Without q, require a coordinate pair and use ST_DWithin on geography with the explicit radius or the 2,000 m Find near me default. Use the GiST index; paginate bounded local candidates and fetch published scoped summaries in one bounded batch. Text results sort by match relevance DESC, optional distance ASC, LocationId ASC; coordinate-only nearby results sort by distance ASC then LocationId ASC. Bind the cursor to that exact sort plus q/coordinates/radius/source and page-size policy; a changed query cannot reuse an old cursor. source=accessmap suppresses provider fallback; Provisional may only appear as a permitted identity with no accessibility label. No suggestion computes compatibility.
Discovery POST accepts {area:{lat,lng,radiusMeters},requiredFeatures:[{featureType,desiredStatus}],preferredFeatures:[{featureType,desiredStatus}],travelingAlone,requestedFloor,pageSize,cursor}. The client sends the visible explicit area/radius: Find near me starts at 2,000 m; manual-area/pin search uses the User-confirmed extent. Validate finite coordinates, positive configured-bounded radius and supported nonduplicate criteria. pageSize initially defaults to 20 and is capped by server configuration. Evaluate only Active local candidates with current published scoped evidence. Order by required-condition coverage, preferred matches DESC, distance ASC, trusted evidence freshness DESC, LocationId ASC. This is suitability ranking, not a promise that distance is always the first criterion. Return reasons and nextCursor without external candidates. Both requiredFeatures and preferredFeatures require desiredStatus=Available; reject Unknown/Limited/NotAvailable or any unsupported value with 422 UNSUPPORTED_DESIRED_STATUS. Apply the same validation to preference PUT and UI presets.
Public search/discovery cursors are opaque integrity-protected continuation tokens bound to normalized q/area/filter hash, source, sort position, policy version and data cutoff. Guest pagination requires no UserId, account or session. A cursor is not an authorization credential and cannot expose private data. Changing criteria starts a new search. Private favorites cursors additionally bind the authenticated owner UserId; another account cannot replay them. Persist no raw server-side search/GPS trail.
Private preference/favorite APIs retain their existing ownership, consent, optimistic version and idempotency contracts. The client may load consented defaults, display/edit them and send the resulting explicit criteria. Empty discovery input is never secretly merged with saved private fields. Favorite and local-recent shortcuts navigate to places; they do not assign compatibility labels.
B.5 Endpoint examples
Text example: GET /api/v1/locations/search?source=accessmap&q=Saigon%20Centre&limit=20. This has no implicit 2 km cutoff. Optional lat/lng may bias ranking without silently restricting text matches. Nearby example: GET /api/v1/locations/search?source=accessmap&lat=10.773820&lng=106.701140&radiusMeters=2000&limit=20. The UI identifies this as Find near me and displays its radius. A suggestion contains {"locationId":"<UUID>","source":"accessmap","name":"Saigon Centre","hasAccessibilityData":true,"label":null}, with a bounded nextCursor when another page exists. No externalPlaceId or provider destination is returned.
Discovery example: POST /api/v1/locations/discover/search with {"area":{"lat":10.77382,"lng":106.70114,"radiusMeters":2000},"requiredFeatures":[{"featureType":"EntranceDoor","desiredStatus":"Available"},{"featureType":"Elevator","desiredStatus":"Available"}],"preferredFeatures":[{"featureType":"AccessibleRestroom","desiredStatus":"Available"}],"travelingAlone":true,"requestedFloor":2,"pageSize":20}. The User explicitly chose these criteria. Return locationId, label, reasons, matchedScopeIds, verified access limits, published feature versions, freshness and cursor. Missing evidence is InsufficientData.
GET /api/v1/map/features?bbox=minLng,minLat,maxLng,maxLat&zoom&layers=places,entrances,advisories returns only bounded approved markers/clusters with source/version and safe counts. GET /api/v1/locations/{id}/surroundings returns approved optional observations/previews or an empty list if no source is implemented. An expired thumbnail link is renewed only after current publication/access checks.
B.6 Business rules and configuration
Use the single shared PlaceSearchDefaultRadiusMeters=2000 setting from WF1 B.4; do not generate a separate FindNearMeDefaultRadiusMeters option. This is the initial nearby-search setting, not a global text-search limit. Text q is unrestricted by that default; any radius filter must be explicit. Manual-area/pin discovery sends its confirmed area/radius. Bound positive radius, pageSize and rows with validated server configuration; discovery initially uses 20 results/page. Match supported canonical features under versioned mappings; adding a type requires the team/developer catalogue change described in A.6.2, not arbitrary Admin tag creation. Keep criterion-specific regulation evidence separate from whole-place suitability.
DiscoveryOptions is the single WF3 configuration authority, consumed by search/discovery/map handlers and their fixtures. Shared PlaceSearchDefaultRadiusMeters=2000 and PlaceSearchMaxResults=20 remain owned by WF1 B.4 and are referenced, not duplicated. All durations use seconds and distances metres unless explicitly stated. Baseline policy version discovery-limits-v1; finite defaults are demo starting bounds, not benchmark guarantees.
DiscoveryOptions.MaxRadiusMeters: integer, default20000, valid1..20000 and >=PlaceSearchDefaultRadiusMeters; applies to every explicitly radius-filtered suggestion/discovery request. Excess returns422 SEARCH_RADIUS_EXCEEDED; text-only search has no implicit radius.
DiscoveryOptions.DefaultPageSize: integer20; MaxPageSize: integer50, valid1..50 with DefaultPageSize<=MaxPageSize. Omitted discovery pageSize uses default; out-of-range values return422 INVALID_PAGE_SIZE. Suggestions remain capped by shared PlaceSearchMaxResults.
DiscoveryOptions.MaxViewportAreaKm2: decimal400, valid>0 and <=400. Validate finite ordered bbox coordinates and compute geographic area; antimeridian-crossing boxes are unsupported and return422 INVALID_VIEWPORT. Excess area returns422 VIEWPORT_TOO_LARGE with a narrow-area prompt.
DiscoveryOptions.MaxMapItemsPerResponse: integer500, valid1..500. A map response contains at most this many authorized markers/clusters across its requested layers. Use deterministic clustering for the supplied zoom followed by stable keyset pagination when needed; return hasMore and nextCursor. Never silently truncate an apparently complete map. Map cursors bind bbox/zoom/layers/policy/sort position; counts include only authorized public records.
DiscoveryOptions.QueryTimeoutSeconds: integer5, valid1..30; bound each search/discovery/map database operation, propagate cancellation and avoid automatic query retries exceeding the request budget. Timeout returns503 SEARCH_QUERY_TIMEOUT with correlationId and no fabricated label or partial-success page.
DiscoveryOptions.CursorTtlSeconds: integer900, valid60..3600. Sign opaque cursors with server-issued expiry and bind normalized filters, sort, policy and data cutoff; expired/tampered/mismatched cursors return422 SEARCH_CURSOR_INVALID and require a new first-page request. Public cursors never require a UserId; private favorite cursors also bind owner.
Validate all options on startup. Oversized requests are rejected before heavy queries; query plans and pagination must bound materialized rows instead of loading all matches into memory. Optional address geocoding remains disabled until its provider, timeout and readiness are explicitly configured; manual pin/local text search remain available. Acceptance covers each exact boundary and over-limit, timeout/cancellation, map pagination without hidden truncation, cursor tampering/expiry/filter changes and shared WF1/WF3 defaults. Record actual benchmark results during implementation; tune values only through a versioned reviewed configuration change. Required feature conditions use AND and compatible scopes; assistance requires evidence, not just a companion toggle. Public map layers remain approved places/features, entrances/floor limits and authorized advisories; sourced surroundings stay disabled/empty until their source, timestamp, permission and update path exist. PostGIS performs bounded queries; the map SDK renders the enabled viewport layers.

B.7 Failure matrix
EX-01 no q or usable center→400 with text/address/pin prompt; GPS denial alone is not an error. EX-02 no saved profile→current explicit criteria or general list. EX-03 known place lacks published criteria→InsufficientData with WF1 contribution CTA. EX-04 local matching component failure→published checklist/null label/degraded only if its data read succeeded; otherwise typed service error. EX-05 missing supported mapped evidence→InsufficientData; invalid catalogue value→422. EX-06 selected-address geocoder failure→retain local text results/existing pin and offer retry/manual selection, never external destination fallback. EX-07 stale/disputed required evidence→warning and withheld strong conclusion, resolved through WF2/WF1 ownership.

B.8 Security and observability
Public Guest/User search and discovery enforce Location visibility, input limits and rate limits; source=accessmap never bypasses permissions. Private preference/favorite actions derive UserId from auth and check ownership, consent, versions and deletion. Approved public thumbnail access rechecks publication/permission on renewal; public DTOs never leak private originals, user/device GPS or storage keys. Provider failure means a concrete map/geocoding call failed or timed out; distinguish it from an empty AccessMap result, invalid input and local rule failure. Log safe operational counts, latency, policy version, cache refresh outcomes and missing-evidence reasons with raw q/address/GPS/preferences redacted. Do not create server-side search/visit trails. Public cursors bind query/filter state; private favorites cursors bind the owner as well. No demographic score or behavior-based recommender is introduced; matching uses the explicit functional conditions.
B.9 Integration tests and done criteria
Verify text-only/manual-pin search without GPS, complete-coordinate validation, the 2,000 m near-me default and no implicit text cutoff. Guest and User can query, paginate, inspect published facts and approved derivatives without a saved profile. source=accessmap never invokes external place fallback; geocoding only resolves a chosen center. Guest protected writes and /me reads return 401. Assert no private/Hidden data leakage and no Guest User row or token creation.
Test deterministic rule matching with AND-required conditions, preferred ranking, Unknown versus NotAvailable, coherent entrance/floor scope, stale/disputed required evidence, per-request companion toggle and insufficient floor data. No Python/remote matcher is invoked. No User-confirmed filter silently becomes a claim or a saved preference write. A local rule failure returns a published checklist only when that read succeeded; data errors are not accessibility labels. WF3 never creates Location/claim/vote/report/reward by reading results.
Test q plus coordinates uses relevance before distance, while coordinate-only nearby uses distance; reject a cursor from different criteria. Test a failing context plus an unresolved alternative => InsufficientData, all relevant contexts affirmatively unusable => Inaccessible, a complete independent context plus an unknown alternative => IndependentAccess, and no verified assistance option => no AssistedAccess even when travelingAlone=false. Assert that Limited plus travelingAlone=false, an approved source claim, an Admin note or an image alone never produces AssistedAccess.
The baseline emits no AssistedAccess without typed supported assistance data and performs no text/image inference during search; return InsufficientData for assistance-dependent uncertainty. A complete independent alternative remains IndependentAccess and all affirmatively unusable relevant contexts remain Inaccessible. Add request/saved-preference validation for Available accepted and Limited/NotAvailable/Unknown rejected with 422; published states remain readable and are evaluated under B.2. Unsupported legacy defaults are not auto-applied.
Single-scope fixtures: EntranceDoor at Entrance A plus Elevator at Floor 2 cannot jointly satisfy one context; parent/child and sibling scopes do not inherit features. Unknown scope identity remains unresolved; requestedFloor uses only a Known Floor scope with exact FloorNumber. All required features in one supported Known scope can satisfy that scoped result; output never claims an unrepresented route. Resolve reviewed merge aliases/scopes consistently and exclude merge-retired feature rows.
Test Contribute for known-place missing evidence and empty results. Retain bounded identity/name/address/pin/scope/feature prompts; Guest must register/sign in as User before protected WF-01 actions, then resume the draft. Never trust filters as claims. Admin mobile login is rejected. WF-01 deduplicates without Hidden/Provisional leakage or automatic unhide. WF-02 owns review/correction; WF-03 displays safe warnings only.
Approved public evidence thumbnails must originate from permitted published media. Expired link→recheck and renew capability; revoked/unpublished media→no renewal. Cache/source version mismatch or expiry→refresh from current approved data; failed optional refresh→omit/mark unavailable, never renew stale facts. Optional surroundings may legitimately return an empty list. A geocoder/map provider failure is a failed external support call, not proof of inaccessible conditions.
Test opt-in preference CRUD, missing/saved state, duplicate/unsupported criteria, stale expectedVersion, visible default prefill and request-only overrides. Test favorite ownership/idempotency/deletion, unchanged first-save CreatedAt, stable paging, merged/inactive targets and 100-item limit. Favorites cursors cannot cross authenticated owners. Public Guest/User search cursors bind to query/filter/sort/policy state and data cutoff without requiring a UserId or session; reject tampered or mismatched criteria/policy tokens. A public cursor never authorizes a private route. Client integration acceptance separately checks device-local recent places: deduplicate, cap at20, expire30 days after latest open and Clear without server sync. Backend acceptance verifies that no server search-history synchronization/storage is introduced; device execution is outside backend-only delivery. Verify raw q/GPS/visit trails are not retained by the search service; current-request processing and explicit saved needs/favorites remain allowed. The current DTO/policy has no demographic scoring input; labels use declared functional conditions, not an inferred age, gender or visit habit.
